{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixSurrealsArchimedean.StandardPartFunctor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixSurrealsArchimedean.StandardPartFunctor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.mass_limit_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.mass_limit_unique","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/standard-part-functor.lean#L89-L99","doc":"Two binding routes that agree in the limit give the same limiting mass —\nthe original claim, now recovered as a corollary of the limit statement rather\nthan assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.mass_error_eq_binding_error","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.mass_error_eq_binding_error","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/standard-part-functor.lean#L79-L87","doc":"**The mass error is exactly the binding error — no amplification.**\n\nThe quantitative companion: whatever discrepancy remains between two binding\nroutes transfers to the predicted mass one-for-one. This is why a factor-2 miss\nin `B_qCLT` is a factor-2 miss in the mass, and it is falsifiable — any\namplifying or damping constant would break the equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.archimedean_mass_commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.archimedean_mass_commutes","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/standard-part-functor.lean#L60-L77","doc":"**The mass evaluation commutes with the `A → ∞` limit.**\n\nIf the exact algebraic binding traces `B A` converge to the macroscopic value\n`B_qCLT` as the scale `A → ∞`, then the bound masses `m_unbound − B A` converge\nto `m_unbound − B_qCLT`.\n\nThis is what `rem:archimedean-functor-trace-commutativity` asserts: the\nstandard-part evaluation passes through the limit. Its content is the\nlimit-interchange, which the previous equality-substitution version never\nstated.\n\n**Conditional**: the convergence `h` is the hypothesis, and it is open — see the\nstatus note at the head of this file. ","signatureChunk":0}]}